  "notes": "Cash basis county. Statement receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Statement 'Taxes' 2,531,544 split using the Statement of Activities general receipts (p2): Property 2,178,349 + Motor vehicle 341,703 + Lodging tax 11,492 = 2,531,544 exactly. 'Local' 623,488 kept as one line (context label). Capital outlay on the statement has no function printed. Fund balances (beginning 6,728,254 / ending 6,661,186) recorded as fund balance; cash (Cash 5,461,405 + Restricted cash 1,199,781) on the balance sheet only, no beginning cash printed (as later years). Balance sheet from the governmental funds Statement of Assets and Fund Balances (p3), whose totals equal the Statement of Net Position (p1, 6,661,186; its Unrestricted 5,461,405 = Committed road maintenance 366,633 + Unassigned 5,094,772). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p7, by department; Taxes split into property and motor vehicle by subtraction, budget not split; supersedes the General Fund column of the combining statement p5), Inheritance Tax Fund column from the General Fund combining statement (p5), Road Fund and ARPA budget schedules (p8-9; ARPA actual 0, budget 625,933), and the nonmajor combining statement per fund (7 funds, p6). Road Fund and 911 Wireless 'Intergovernmental' kept as other state aid (no grantor printed). Transfers: fund-level in 266,622 = out 266,622 (General 51,425 in, Inheritance 251,425 out, Road 200,000 in, 911 Holding 15,197 in, 911 Wireless 13,370 out, 911 Emergency 1,827 out); the statement p4 shows 200,000 after netting transfers within the General Fund and within nonmajor funds. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
